              "status": "draft-review",
              "wordCount": 262,
              "text": "Sam had a plan for the day. The main job involved the coin. A cat sat near the path while Sam checked a small map. The map showed where the soil and the boil should go. First, Sam picked up the foil and set it beside the join. A pig came close and watched. Sam gave it a pat and went back to the job. Next, the point had to be moved. It was not far, but it was in the wrong place. Sam carried it past the shed and put it by the joint. A light wind came across camp. The moist tipped, but Sam caught it before it fell. Then Sam sat for a short rest and had a snack. The dog stayed nearby. After the rest, Sam checked the coin, the foil, and the point. All three were set. The sun came back, but it did not get in the way. Sam still had one last task. The coil had to go beside the voice. Sam did the job step by step and did not rush. At last, the path was clear and the work was done. The red sat on a mat. The fish rested by the shed. Sam smiled. It had been a busy day, but the plan had worked. Sam gave the coin one last look. The soil stayed in place, and the boil did not tip. A small foil was still by the path. Sam moved it back beside the join. The cat came close again. Sam gave it a pat and checked the point."
